1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,043
The doctor just read six name tags.

2
00:00:03,493 --> 00:00:06,537
Nobody asked the engineer to do that.

3
00:00:06,987 --> 00:00:08,726
Nobody asked the ship.

4
00:00:09,176 --> 00:00:16,133
It was her job, on her list, and when she finished it something happened for everyone.

5
00:00:16,583 --> 00:00:21,800
That is a side story: a quest that belongs to one person.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,043
A new section, at the very end.

7
00:00:26,493 --> 00:00:29,537
Side Stories, and the key is side_stories.

8
00:00:29,987 --> 00:00:31,291
Keep that key.

9
00:00:31,741 --> 00:00:33,480
Inside it, a quest.

10
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:39,148
You know every line of this from Class 1 except the first.

11
00:00:39,598 --> 00:00:40,902
For, colon, medical.

12
00:00:41,352 --> 00:00:49,178
That is a job word, the same word that is on the doctor's Roles line in your roster.

13
00:00:49,628 --> 00:00:52,237
This quest is not the ship's.

14
00:00:52,687 --> 00:00:53,991
It is hers.

15
00:00:54,441 --> 00:01:00,528
Starts when: at once, because I want it running the moment she has it.

16
00:01:00,978 --> 00:01:09,239
Leave that out and she is handed a story that is asleep, and nothing ever wakes it. An objective.

17
00:01:09,689 --> 00:01:11,863
And Done when: signal names_read.

18
00:01:12,313 --> 00:01:14,487
A signal I just invented.

19
00:01:14,937 --> 00:01:17,111
Something has to send it.

20
00:01:18,311 --> 00:01:22,224
Here is the choice only the doctor is offered.

21
00:01:22,674 --> 00:01:26,152
After the semicolon it already says learn suits.

22
00:01:26,602 --> 00:01:29,646
I add a comma, then signal names_read.

23
00:01:30,096 --> 00:01:38,357
Two things happen now when she takes it: the party learns the fact, and her story hears its signal.

24
00:01:38,807 --> 00:01:40,546
Look at this comma.

25
00:01:40,996 --> 00:01:47,517
If I forget it, the signal is never sent, and lint will not tell me.

26
00:01:47,967 --> 00:01:54,924
I am going to show you that in a few minutes, because you will do it.

27
00:01:56,124 --> 00:02:03,515
The game does not hand these stories out by itself, so there is a card. Two parts.

28
00:02:03,965 --> 00:02:11,357
The first goes under the line from Lecture 2 that starts shared BOARDING_SCENES, with the same indent.

29
00:02:11,807 --> 00:02:15,285
It reads my new section and keeps it.

30
00:02:15,735 --> 00:02:20,083
The second goes at the very end of the file.

31
00:02:20,533 --> 00:02:27,054
It says: every time somebody beams down, hand them the story that is for them.

32
00:02:27,504 --> 00:02:30,113
I change nothing on this card.

33
00:02:30,563 --> 00:02:31,867
I paste it.

34
00:02:32,317 --> 00:02:41,448
Lint is clean, and I have to be honest about what that means here: lint cannot see this card at all.

35
00:02:41,898 --> 00:02:46,246
If I paste half of it, lint still says clean.

36
00:02:47,446 --> 00:02:50,489
The chief gets one too. For: engineering.

37
00:02:50,939 --> 00:02:53,983
Find out how the core was stopped.

38
00:02:54,433 --> 00:02:58,780
And the choice only he is offered sends the signal.

39
00:02:59,230 --> 00:03:00,970
Same shape, different job.

40
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:03,159
Two people, two stories.

41
00:03:04,359 --> 00:03:11,750
A side story can lead somewhere, and it does it the way every quest does: with Then.

42
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:15,678
When the doctor's story finishes, it sends names_known.

43
00:03:16,128 --> 00:03:22,650
And up here, in the ship's own quests, a new one: Account for the Crew.

44
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:27,883
Scope: shared, running from the start, done when it hears names_known.

45
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:30,072
So read the chain.

46
00:03:30,522 --> 00:03:32,261
She reads the tags.

47
00:03:32,711 --> 00:03:34,450
That finishes her story.

48
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:37,509
Her story finishes the ship's quest.

49
00:03:37,959 --> 00:03:39,698
One waits, one sends.

50
00:03:40,148 --> 00:03:42,322
Notice where the reward is.

51
00:03:42,772 --> 00:03:44,511
On the ship's quest.

52
00:03:44,961 --> 00:03:49,743
A reward written on a side story is paid to nobody.

53
00:03:50,193 --> 00:03:55,411
And one thing you will see in other people's files: Leads to.

54
00:03:55,861 --> 00:04:02,817
That points a person at a thing on a map, or a place in a ruin.

55
00:04:03,267 --> 00:04:08,050
We have rooms, not a map, so it does nothing here.

56
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:10,674
We will use it later.

57
00:04:11,874 --> 00:04:12,874
Five rules.

58
00:04:13,324 --> 00:04:21,585
A side story is a bonus: nobody covers for a person, so never hang the main story on one.

59
00:04:22,035 --> 00:04:27,252
One job word in three places: the roster, the story, the choice.

60
00:04:27,702 --> 00:04:30,311
Name the job, not the person.

61
00:04:30,761 --> 00:04:33,370
No reward on a side story.

62
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:36,863
And one story goes to one person.

63
00:04:37,313 --> 00:04:44,270
Now lint, and I am going to start with the two it misses. The comma. Clean.

64
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:46,893
That story can never finish.

65
00:04:47,343 --> 00:04:49,952
A misspelled job on For. Clean.

66
00:04:50,402 --> 00:04:53,011
That story is handed to nobody.

67
00:04:53,461 --> 00:04:56,070
Those two you check by eye.

68
00:04:56,520 --> 00:05:04,780
Here is what it does catch: a signal name that does not match, two warnings, one from each end.

69
00:05:05,230 --> 00:05:09,578
And a section key the card is not looking for.

70
00:05:10,778 --> 00:05:13,822
Before we go: the ship's quest list.

71
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:16,880
Account for the Crew is waiting.

72
00:05:17,330 --> 00:05:19,504
Both of them beam down.

73
00:05:19,954 --> 00:05:22,128
The doctor reads the tags.

74
00:05:22,578 --> 00:05:26,926
Back on the bridge: quest complete, twice, and the reward.

75
00:05:27,376 --> 00:05:31,289
Now the same mission with the doctor left behind.

76
00:05:31,739 --> 00:05:35,652
The chief is offered her reading, marked as covering.

77
00:05:36,102 --> 00:05:37,407
He takes it.

78
00:05:37,857 --> 00:05:40,030
The party learns the fact.

79
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:42,654
And on the bridge, nothing.

80
00:05:43,104 --> 00:05:47,452
Her story was never handed out, because she never came.

81
00:05:47,902 --> 00:05:49,641
That is rule one.

82
00:05:50,841 --> 00:05:58,233
Your third crew member gets a story of their own, finished by the reading you gave them.

83
00:05:58,683 --> 00:06:01,726
Give the chief's story somewhere to lead.

84
00:06:02,176 --> 00:06:12,611
Then break it on purpose: misspell the job on For, watch lint say clean, and play it once to see what does not happen.

85
00:06:13,061 --> 00:06:20,452
Next time you put all of it together, and play ten minutes of your own away mission.
